Title: "If"
Id: "7d6d964a-7f0d-443a-92e4-4b1cd4cf4d56"

Text: "`if:` assumes its condition and checks the `then:` clauses in that context.

```mlg-fragment
if: P
then: Q
```

The group may have an optional label heading. Nested clauses use the same clause syntax recursively.

Both `if:` and `then:` are statement positions: a bare `is` or `\\:...:/` specification is rejected. Use the predicate forms `is?` / `is_not?` and `\\:...?:/`.

```mlg-fragment
if: x is? \\set
then: f(x) is? \\real
```"
Id: "f3e1b6b4-ed15-4f98-84fe-3ef5fb883fc8"
